<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan tenders to sell diesel lifting July 2-19.</title>
<headline>Taiwan tenders to sell diesel lifting July 2-19.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 225,000-250,000 barrels of 0.3-percent sulphur diesel for July 2-19 delivery, free-on-board (fob) Kaohsiung, a CPC official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on June 9 and bids will be valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last tender, Taiwan sold two 225,000-to-250,000-barrel cargoes of diesel for June 4-17 lifting at around $24.60 per barrel, fob Kaohsiung.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3084)</p>
